From: GCC Toolset Maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: Fix allocator lookup in stacktrace max_size

The DTS 12 GCC 12.2.1 source snapshot contains the upstream stacktrace
implementation with max_size() looking for the allocator inside _Impl.  The
allocator belongs to basic_stacktrace itself, so instantiating max_size() fails
to compile.  Keep the upstream implementation and correct that member lookup.

--- a/libstdc++-v3/include/std/stacktrace
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/include/std/stacktrace
@@ -476 +476 @@
-      { return _Impl::_S_max_size(_M_impl._M_alloc); }
+      { return _Impl::_S_max_size(_M_alloc); }
